  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of species from the following which have square pyramidal structure is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>BrF</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>IF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ICl</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Among the given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>IF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;have squre pyramidal structure.&nbsp; VSEPR&nbsp;theory helps us to predict the shape of molecules from the number of electron pairs and lone pairs of electrons that surrounds the central atoms.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0104_11448cb43ae3.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 188px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0104_8a722efb578d.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 207px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0104_bda4261f9c6b.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 183px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
  }
